WEBVTT

m1
00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:05.350
The fight pauses at a Choose. The handler holds the rest of the fight as k.

m2
00:00:05.900 --> 00:00:12.850
To answer, it runs battle itself: the same function a person plays. It needs no model of the game.

m3.1
00:00:13.400 --> 00:00:18.317
For each card it can play, and for ending the turn, it plays that card on the state.

m3.2
00:00:18.317 --> 00:00:21.650
Then it starts a new battle from that state, three times.

m4
00:00:22.200 --> 00:00:29.300
Each new battle runs on a stack of its own. None of them touches k, so the paused fight keeps its dice.

m5
00:00:29.850 --> 00:00:37.350
The handler counts the wins. Here every move wins all three. The paused fight has not moved.

m6.1
00:00:37.900 --> 00:00:40.917
With a tie it keeps the first move, Bash.

m6.2
00:00:40.917 --> 00:00:47.400
It resumes k with it, once: in doeff, k can be resumed only one time. The fight goes on.

m7.1
00:00:47.950 --> 00:00:53.733
On seed 3, the bot answers eleven Chooses with a hundred and sixty-five playouts,

m7.2
00:00:53.733 --> 00:00:55.800
in about a fifth of a second.
